# Brand & Copy

## ViraStack products

- **Lockup:** Products are always `ViraStack` + short name: `ViraStack Start`, `ViraStack AI`, `ViraStack Mask`, `ViraStack Password`, `ViraStack Guide`, `ViraStack Academy`. Never the short name alone in body copy (dense navigation is the only exception).
- **Implementation:** Use rich-text tags backed by `guideProductTags` / `GuideProductMark` (`<start>Start</start>`). Never write the lockup as plain text in JSON.
- **Academy:** Not a `ProductId`; use a local rich handler with brand span + bold name, colored from `brandPalettes` (id `academy`).
- **Colors:** Read from `src/config/brand-palettes.config.ts` (single source; exposed as `text-brand-<id>` / `bg-brand-<id>-solid`). Never hardcode a product color. `ViraStack`'s own turquoise (`virastackColor`) colors the logo mark only; no product may use that hue.
- **Icons:** Read from `src/config/product-icons.config.ts` (Lucide). One icon per product.
- **Repeats:** Do not repeat the lockup needlessly; prefer one lockup per sentence or list.

## Technology names

- React, Next.js, TanStack Start, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui and similar are labeled with `AcademyBadge` (icon badge), not plain text.
- Valid `kind` values and labels: `src/features/academy/constants/badge.constants.ts`.
- In rich text, expose a handler per tech (`<react>React</react>` → `<AcademyBadge kind="react" />`).

## Emphasis

- **Bold:** key phrase or takeaway.
- **Italic:** foreign or quoted word only. Product short names are never italic and always in the product color, in every context.
- **Weights (two tiers):** Display (hero lockup): `ViraStack` `font-black` + product name `font-black`. UI (header, footer, search, running text): `ViraStack` `font-semibold` + product name `font-bold`.
- **ViraStack color:** always `text-primary` (never `text-foreground`); the outlined wordmark is neutral decoration.
- **Hero lockup:** big heroes show the outlined `ViraStack` wordmark (`BrandLockup`) above the black product name (Display tier).
- **Icons:** only through badges, not inline decoration.

## Sources

- Link to `/academy/sources` when describing how sources are chosen; the criteria live there.
